@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# ReXGlue Optimization & Performance Architecture Report
+**Target Title**: Blitz: The League II (`4D5707E8`) & Shared ReXGlue SDK (`rexglue-sdk`)  
+**ReXGlue Version**: v0.10.0.9-dev  
+**Build Target**: Windows x86-64 / Zen 4 (`-march=znver4`, AVX-512/AVX2/FMA/MOVBE)  
+**Baseline Commit**: `f5337cd` -> **Argon High Head**: `2499f07` (`rexglue-sdk`) / `7c78e83` (`blitz2`)  
+
+---
+
+## Executive Summary
+
+This report documents both the initial optimization pass (Phases 1?7) and the **Argon High Architecture & SDK Reconciliation Audit**, which unified Peggle 2 and Blitz 2 SDK timing/menu/audio changes, hardened GPU command-list/memory state safety, implemented an asynchronous DXIL/PSO worker pool with a persistent disk PSO cache (`pso_disk_cache.bin`), optimized on-field EDRAM resolves and FP16 shader math (`handheld_gpu_fastpath`), and upgraded PowerPC VMX128 / big-endian codegen to native Zen 4 AVX-512 / AVX2 / `MOVBE` intrinsics.
+
+---
+
+## Argon High Architecture & SDK Reconciliation Report
+
+### 1. ReXGlue SDK & Git History Reconciliation (Peggle 2 + Blitz 2)
+
+1. **Unified Zero-Jitter Hybrid Frame Pacer (`display_refresh_rate` / `target_fps`)**:
+   - *Conflict*: Peggle 2 introduced a hybrid sleep-spin pacer in `src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp` using `target_fps` while Blitz 2 used a separate 1 ms `SDL_Delay` loop on `display_refresh_rate` alongside `VdSwap` rate-limiting (`target_frame_rate`).
+   - *Fix*: Unified host presentation pacing in `SDLWindowedAppContext::RunMainLoop` (`src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp`) into a single high-resolution `steady_clock` hybrid sleep-spin pacer (sleeping until `remaining - 1.5 ms`, then `_mm_pause()` spin-waiting to the exact sub-microsecond deadline). Bidirectional synchronization keeps `display_refresh_rate` and `target_fps` consistent (`0` = Auto/Match Display Hz, or `60`/`72`/`120`/`144` Hz), while `VdSwap` in `src/kernel/xboxkrnl/xboxkrnl_video.cpp` enforces the 60.0 Hz guest simulation step.
+2. **Guest Logic Step & 49.875 MHz Timebase Integrity**:
+   - *Conflict*: Need to ensure Peggle 2's 1/60s guest logic step never warps `mftb` (`49,875,000 Hz`) or `KeQueryPerformanceCounter`.
+   - *Fix*: Verified `Clock::guest_tick_frequency_platform()` (`src/core/clock.cpp`) remains locked at `49,875,000 Hz` (`100 ns` ticks via `compute_qpc_time` 128-bit integer math). Fixed a race/drift bug in `InitializeVideoSystem` (`src/kernel/xboxkrnl/xboxkrnl_video.cpp`) where `vd_global_vblank_counter` was incremented inside the 60 Hz timer callback in addition to `CommandProcessor::OnPrimaryBufferEnd` (`src/graphics/command_processor.cpp`), which double-counted VBlanks (~120 Hz) during active rendering. The timer callback now only advances `vd_global_vblank_counter` while the GPU command processor has not yet taken over (`last_swap_time_ns == 0`).
+3. **Unified Menu & Hotkey Architecture (`F1` / `F3` / `F4` / `F8` / `F9` / `F10` / `F11`)**:
+   - *Conflict*: Peggle 2 added a second top menu bar (`DrawSettingsBar`) in `rex_app.cpp` with duplicate `F1`/`F3`/`F11` bindings that conflicted with `qol_ui.h` (`DrawQoLMenu`) and Blitz 2's `OnKeyDown` hotkeys.
+   - *Fix*: Consolidated all QoL settings, display/presenter options, audio controls, and handheld GPU fastpath toggles into `rex::ui::DrawQoLMenu` (`include/rex/ui/qol_ui.h`) with a single shared hotkey layout:
+     - `F1`: Toggle ReXGlue QoL Top Menu Bar & Settings Window.
+     - `F3`: Toggle Live Telemetry Overlay (`Host Present FPS`, `Rendered FPS`, `Guest Logic FPS`, `FrameSkip`, `FastPath`, `Refresh`).
+     - `F4`: Toggle CRT Post-Processing Filter.
+     - `F8`: Reset Guest Physics Timing & Audio Clocks (`rex::graphics::ResetTimingState()`).
+     - `F9`: Toggle Adaptive Frame-Skip (`adaptive_frameskip`).
+     - `F10`: Cycle Host Display Refresh Rate (`Auto -> 60 -> 72 -> 120 -> 144 Hz`).
+     - `F11` / `Alt+Enter`: Toggle Fullscreen.
+4. **Clean Separation of Title-Specific Workarounds**:
+   - Isolated Peggle 2's XMA stream clear-wait bypass behind `REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(xma_ignore_clear_wait, false, ...)` in `src/audio/xma/context.cpp` (default `false` so Blitz 2 cutscenes and commentary streams never read partially decoded ringbuffers).
+   - Isolated `REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(audio_force_mute, false, ...)` in `src/audio/sdl/sdl_audio_driver.cpp`.
+
+---
+
+### 2. Audit & Hardening of 3.8 Flash's Blitz 2 & SDK Changes
+
+1. **`DeferredCommandList` Dirty-State Tracking Bug Fix (`src/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.cpp`)**:
+   - *Bug*: `kD3DSetPipelineState` updated `last_pipeline_state` without clearing `last_pipeline_state_handle`, and `kSetPipelineStateHandle` updated `last_pipeline_state_handle` without clearing `last_pipeline_state`. Alternating between raw `ID3D12PipelineState*` (clear/resolve/blit passes) and cached PSO handles (`D3D12PipelineCache`) caused false cache hits (`handle == last_pipeline_state_handle`), silently dropping `SetPipelineState` calls and corrupting geometry draws after resolves.
+   - *Fix*: `kD3DSetPipelineState` now zeroes `last_pipeline_state_handle`, and `kSetPipelineStateHandle` zeroes `last_pipeline_state`. Verified state cache invalidation occurs on every `Reset()` (`BeginSubmission`).
+2. **Command Processor & `adaptive_frameskip` State Safety (`src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp`)**:
+   - *Bug*: On skipped frames (`skip_gpu_draw_ == true`), `IssueSwap` bypassed `EndSubmission(true)` when `!submission_open_`, which prevented `submission_completed_` fence progression, deferred deletion retirement, and `frame_open_` closure.
+   - *Fix*: `IssueSwap` now always invokes `EndSubmission(true)` so frame fences, ringbuffers, and resource lifetimes advance deterministically even on skipped frames.
+3. **Upload Ring-Buffer & `TrimUnusedPages` Use-After-Free Fix (`src/ui/graphics_upload_buffer_pool.cpp`)**:
+   - *Bug*: `TrimUnusedPages(size_t keep_count)` deleted pages from `writable_page_list_`, which holds the currently mapped page actively being written by the current open submission (`current_frame_Used_bytes_` offsets).
+   - *Fix*: Re-architected `TrimUnusedPages` to NEVER delete from `writable_page_list_` (only at most one active page is ever in `writable_page_list_`) and instead only evict surplus retired pages from `flushed_page_list_` whose GPU submission fence (`last_submission_number_ <= completed_submission_`) has already completed on the GPU.
+4. **VRAM LRU Eviction & Placed-Resource Heap Aliasing Safety (`src/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.cpp`)**:
+   - *Bug*: `EnforceVRAMLimit` destroyed evicted `D3D12Texture` instances and returned their 64 MB `D3D12HeapPool` chunk slots (`heap_pool_->Free`) as soon as `last_usage_time` was old, without checking whether the GPU had finished executing `texture->last_usage_submission`! Reallocating that heap range for a new placed texture aliased in-flight GPU memory.
+   - *Fix*: Added `uint64_t last_usage_submission` to `Texture` (`include/rex/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.h`) and gated `EnforceVRAMLimit` on `d3d_tex->last_usage_submission <= completed_submission`.
+
+---
+
+### 3. Asynchronous Shader Compilation & Persistent Disk PSO Cache
+
+1. **Lock-Free Async PSO Compilation Lookup & Fallback (`src/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp`)**:
+   - Eliminated synchronous `creation_completion_event_->Wait()` render-thread stalls inside `ConfigurePipeline` when an async PSO is still compiling on the background worker pool.
+   - Added `PipelineRuntime::ready` (`std::atomic<bool>` with acquire/release semantics) set by `CreateD3D12Pipeline` before storing `pipeline->handle`.
+   - For non-essential geometry draws whose PSO is still compiling (`!ready`), `GetPipelineStateByHandle` returns `nullptr` and `CommandProcessor::IssueDraw` cleanly skips only that unready draw call without stalling the 60 Hz frame or corrupting bound vertex/constant state, while depth/color EDRAM resolves and post-processing passes remain synchronous.
+2. **Persistent Disk PSO & DXIL Cache (`pso_disk_cache.bin`)**:
+   - Implemented binary serialization (`PSODiskCacheEntryHeader`, magic `0x314F5350` `'PSO1'`) in `D3D12PipelineCache` (`include/rex/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.h`, `src/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp`).
+   - On startup (`Initialize`), `LoadDiskCache()` pre-warms all previously compiled `PipelineDescription` + vertex/pixel DXIL blobs from `pso_disk_cache.bin`, deduplicating shaders by `ucode_data_hash` + modification bits and queuing PSO creation on the worker pool before the first frame renders.
+   - Newly compiled pipelines are appended incrementally (`AppendToDiskCache`) and flushed cleanly on `Shutdown()`.
+
+---
+
+### 4. On-Field GPU Bottleneck Reduction (EDRAM & Weather Fast-Path)
+
+1. **`handheld_gpu_fastpath` CVar & UI Toggle**:
+   - Added `REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(handheld_gpu_fastpath, ...)` in `src/graphics/flags.cpp` (default `true` when `REX_BUILD_LEGION_GO` is defined, toggleable live in the `F1` QoL Menu under Display & Window and shown in the `F3` telemetry overlay).
+2. **EDRAM Resolve & Render-Target Bandwidth Optimizations (`src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp`, `src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp`)**:
+   - Coalesced UAV barriers during EDRAM resolve clear loops (emitting a single post-clear UAV barrier instead of redundant pre+post barriers when clear and resolve dispatches are separated by RTV/DSV/SRV state transitions).
+   - Added an early-out in `CommandProcessor::IssueCopy` when `handheld_gpu_fastpath` is enabled to skip redundant back-to-back EDRAM resolves (`last_resolve_key_` matching source EDRAM base, pitch, format, and destination guest address/format with zero intervening draws or clears).
+   - Added `GetOrCreateResolveTargetTexture` single-copy resolve fast-path when destination guest memory already holds an up-to-date texture matching the resolve geometry and format.
+3. **Relaxed Half-Precision (`min16float`) Pixel Shader Fast-Path (`src/graphics/d3d12/shader_translator.cpp`)**:
+   - When `handheld_gpu_fastpath` is active, pixel shaders that do not write depth (`!writes_depth()`) compile with `-HV 2018` and `#define float4 min16float4` / `float3 min16float3` / `float2 min16float2` (preserving full 32-bit `float` for interpolants, constant buffers, and vertex shaders), doubling RDNA 3 (Ryzen Z1 Extreme) VALU throughput and cutting VGPR pressure on heavy rain, mud, and turf shaders.
+
+---
+
+### 5. PowerPC VMX128-to-AVX-512 / AVX2 & `MOVBE` Intrinsic Optimization
+
+1. **Hardware `MOVBE` Big-Endian Memory Access (`include/rex/ppc/context.h`, `resources/templates/codegen/pch_h.inja`, `resources/templates/test/ppc_config_h.inja`)**:
+   - Replaced `__builtin_bswap16/32/64(*(volatile u16/32/64*)(...))` (which prevented Clang from folding volatile loads/stores into `MOVBE` and evaluated address expressions multiple times) with single-evaluation `rex_raw_addr(base, addr)` and `rex::ppc::load_be_u16/32/64` / `store_be_u16/32/64` using hardware `_loadbe_i16/32/64` and `_storebe_i16/32/64` (`movbe` instruction on Zen 4 / x86-64).
+   - Updated `stack.h` and `function.h` to use `load_be_u32` and `store_be_u16/32/64`.
+2. **Zen 4 AVX-512 / AVX2 VMX128 Intrinsics (`include/rex/ppc/intrinsics.h`, `src/codegen/builders/vector.cpp`, `src/codegen/builders/memory.cpp`)**:
+   - **`vperm` (`simde_mm_perm_epi8_`)**: Upgraded to single-instruction Zen 4 AVX-512 VBMI `_mm_permutex2var_epi8` (`vpermt2b`) when `__AVX512VBMI__ && __AVX512VL__` are enabled.
+   - **`vcfux` (`simde_mm_cvtepu32_ps_`)**: Upgraded to single-instruction AVX-512VL `_mm_cvtepu32_ps` (`vcvtudq2ps`).
+   - **`vslo` / `vsro` (`simde_mm_vslo` / `simde_mm_vsro`)**: Replaced stack-spill + `memset` + `memcpy` implementations with pure branchless `simde_mm_shuffle_epi8` (`pshufb`).
+   - **`stvlx` / `stvrx` (`simde_mm_stvlx` / `simde_mm_stvrx`)**: Replaced byte-by-byte scalar `for` loops with AVX-512BW masked unaligned stores `_mm_mask_storeu_epi8` (`vmovdqu8`) and `pshufb` + `pblendvb` fallback, preserving page-boundary safety when `offset == 0`.
+   - **Variable Vector Shifts & Rotates (`vrlw`, `vsraw`, `vsrw`, `vsrb`, `vsrab`, `vslh`, `vsrh`, `vsrah`)**: Vectorized all scalar loops using AVX-512VL `_mm_rolv_epi32` (`vprolvd`), `_mm_sllv/srlv/srav_epi16`, 256-bit widened `epi8` shifts, and `_mm_srav/srlv_epi32`.
+   - **Saturating Word Add/Sub & Unsigned Pack/Unpack (`vaddsws`, `vsubsws`, `vpkuhus`, `vpkuwus`, `vupkd3d128`)**: Vectorized `vsubsws`, `vpkuhus` (`min_epu16` + `packus_epi16`), `vpkuwus` (`min_epu32` + `packus_epi32`), and `vupkd3d128` (`D3DCOLOR` `pshufb` + `por` and `NORMSHORT4` `pmovsxwd` + `paddd`).
+   - **Deterministic Physics Preservation**: Kept `vmaddfp` and `vnmsubfp` as two-step `mul_ps` + `add_ps`/`sub_ps` (`-ffp-contract=off`) so IEEE rounding and tackle/ball physics remain 100% deterministic, while using hardware FMA (`simde_mm_fmadd_ps_`) for `vexptefp` minimax polynomial evaluation.
+
+---
+
+## Previous Optimization Phases (1?7 Summary)
+
+- **Phase 1**: Frame-skip command list closure & fence signaling (`IssueSwap` calls `EndSubmission(true)`), `new_guest_frame_ready_` atomic pacing, launcher event pump responsiveness.
+- **Phase 2**: Configurable host refresh rate (`0`, `60`, `72`, `120`, `144` Hz), `F9`/`F10` hotkeys, and `F3` telemetry overlay.
+- **Phase 3**: Redundant D3D12 state filtering in `DeferredCommandList::Execute()`, persistent ring-buffer constant uploads, and zero-allocation 64-bit `XXH3_64bits` pipeline hashing.
+- **Phase 4**: Thread priority & ideal processor scheduling (Core 0 PPC main thread, Core 2 GPU CommandProcessor, highest priority audio/XMA, below-normal async PSO workers), `REX_ALWAYS_INLINE` byte swapping, and PM4 `[[likely]]` annotations.
+- **Phase 5**: `GraphicsUploadBufferPool::TrimUnusedPages` and periodic `IDXGIDevice3::Trim()` every 120 frames / scene transitions.
+- **Phase 6**: Coalesced `VdBlockUntilVerticalBlank` and `VdSwap` sleeps to eliminate 30 FPS double-sleep; true GPU render-time gating (`last_frame_gpu_render_ms` & `last_frame_draw_call_count`) for `adaptive_frameskip`.
+- **Phase 7**: Persistent `last_valid_guest_frontbuffer_resource_` caching in `D3D12Presenter` / `VulkanPresenter` to eliminate `FLIP_DISCARD` black-frame flicker on skipped frames, paired with the `physics_time_debt_ms` accumulator.
